<div class="aq-page">
<section class="aq-section"><div class="aq-in aq-stack-l"><header class="aq-sec-head"><h2 class="aq-h1">From protocol to release, then SAT</h2></header><div class="aq-plate aq-plate--block"><ol class="aq-steps aq-steps--hold" style="--cols:4"><li class="aq-steps__st"><span class="aq-steps__n" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div class="aq-steps__body"><h3 class="aq-steps__t">Draft protocol</h3><p class="aq-steps__d">From the approved functional specification, sent <span class="aq-ph">[protocol issue before FAT, weeks]</span> ahead. Every test case has an acceptance criterion and a URS reference.</p></div><span class="aq-steps__run is-valve" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="aq-steps__valve" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6 L21 18 L21 6 L3 18 Z"></path><path d="M12 12 V3 M7 3 H17"></path></svg></span></li><li class="aq-steps__st is-hold"><span class="aq-steps__n" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div class="aq-steps__body"><h3 class="aq-steps__t">Your review and approval</h3><p class="aq-steps__d">Your validation team comments and may add test cases (Annex 15, 2.6); we answer in writing. Nothing runs before your quality unit signs.</p><p class="aq-steps__hold"><span class="aq-steps__stamp"><span class="aq-steps__stamp-k">Hold</span> <span class="aq-steps__who">Signed by your quality unit</span></span></p></div><span class="aq-steps__run" aria-hidden="true"></span></li><li class="aq-steps__st"><span class="aq-steps__n" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div class="aq-steps__body"><h3 class="aq-steps__t">Internal dry run</h3><p class="aq-steps__d">We run the full protocol ourselves first and fix what it finds, so the witnessed FAT confirms the system rather than debugs it.</p></div><span class="aq-steps__run" aria-hidden="true"></span></li><li class="aq-steps__st is-eol"><span class="aq-steps__n" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div class="aq-steps__body"><h3 class="aq-steps__t">Witnessed execution</h3><p class="aq-steps__d">On our floor, remote or both. Results recorded as found, raw data attached, fabrication hold points already closed.</p></div><span class="aq-steps__run" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="aq-steps__turn" aria-hidden="true"></span></li><li class="aq-steps__ret" aria-hidden="true"></li><li class="aq-steps__st is-bol"><span class="aq-steps__n" aria-hidden="true">05</span><div class="aq-steps__body"><h3 class="aq-steps__t">Deviations and punch list</h3><p class="aq-steps__d">A failed acceptance criterion is a deviation: investigated, fixed, retested (Annex 15, 2.8). A defect that changes no result goes on the punch list.</p></div><span class="aq-steps__run is-valve" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="aq-steps__valve" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6 L21 18 L21 6 L3 18 Z"></path><path d="M12 12 V3 M7 3 H17"></path></svg></span><span class="aq-steps__turn aq-steps__turn--in" aria-hidden="true"></span></li><li class="aq-steps__st is-hold"><span class="aq-steps__n" aria-hidden="true">06</span><div class="aq-steps__body"><h3 class="aq-steps__t">Report and release to ship</h3><p class="aq-steps__d">Signed by both parties. Open deviations ship only on a quality-unit-approved no-impact assessment. Skid drained, then <span class="aq-ph">[post-FAT drying and sealing method]</span>.</p><p class="aq-steps__hold"><span class="aq-steps__stamp"><span class="aq-steps__stamp-k">Hold</span> <span class="aq-steps__who">Signed by both parties</span></span></p></div><span class="aq-steps__run" aria-hidden="true"></span></li><li class="aq-steps__st"><span class="aq-steps__n" aria-hidden="true">07</span><div class="aq-steps__body"><h3 class="aq-steps__t">SAT on your site</h3><p class="aq-steps__d">Critical tests re-run on your feed water, utilities and loop, conductivity read uncompensated (USP &lt;645&gt; stage 1). Then handed to IQ/OQ.</p></div></li></ol><div class="aq-plate__block" aria-hidden="true"><span>Aquemi</span><span>Process</span></div></div></div></section>
</div>
<div class="aq-page">
<section class="aq-section"><div class="aq-in aq-stack-l"><header class="aq-sec-head"><h2 class="aq-h1">What each stage proves</h2><p class="aq-lead">One commissioning and qualification (C&amp;Q) plan covers every stage.</p></header><ol class="aq-rows aq-steps"><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Commissioning</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Flush, pressure test, sanitization, start-up, punch list.</p></div></li><li><a class="aq-rows__row" href="#svc-fat-sat" data-wp="svc-fat-sat"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Factory and site acceptance tests (FAT and SAT)</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Tested with water before shipping, then on your utilities.</p></a></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Installation qualification (IQ)</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Installed as designed: drawings, materials, joints, slopes, instruments.</p></div></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">04</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Operational qualification (OQ)</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Operating limits and worst case tested.</p></div></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">05</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Performance qualification (PQ)</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Required quality, reproducibly, across the seasons.</p></div></li><li><div class="aq-rows__row"><span class="aq-index" aria-hidden="true">06</span><h3 class="aq-rows__t">Periodic review</h3><p class="aq-rows__d">Yearly review of data and changes; requalify where they point.</p></div></li></ol></div></section>
</div>
